# Production. Overlays .env; only the differences belong here.
#
# Loaded when APP_ENV=prod, which the container image sets by way of
# deploy/compose.yaml.
#
# Almost nothing is here on purpose. A production deployment differs from the
# defaults in ways that are specific to it - the database, the domain, the
# passwords - and those belong in the environment, not in a file baked into the
# image. See deploy/.env.example.
#
# The limits and the log level are not missing either: they are administered
# under Settings, which stores them in the database, and what is stored beats
# any file. Written here they would be the copy that loses and goes stale.
#
# TLS is enabled through deploy/compose.tls.yaml rather than here, because
# TLS_ENABLED without TLS_DOMAINS achieves nothing but an error on every start,
# and TLS_DOMAINS cannot be known in advance.
